<title>POLAND: Poland to increase forest area.</title>
<headline>Poland to increase forest area.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's government approved a long-term programme on Tuesday which provides for increasing the area of forest by some 1.6 million hectares so that it covers 33 percent of the country's territory.</p>
<p>Under the scheme, the state forest offices will seed new trees on non-farming land to increase the forest area from the current 28 percent of the Polish territory to 30 percent in 2020 and one third in the middle of the next century, the government said in a statement.</p>
<p>Although Poland has a lot of forest compared with other European countries, trees are weak in many areas hit by air pollution.</p>
</text>
